{"title":"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ratio of the number of girls to the number of boys in a class of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/41281174060fd95dee9dac239ba24691436e388b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:5$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />. How many fewer girls than boys are in the class?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6a5669a202b4b451ef53a723a1ba92cfd3f1a52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 6 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let there be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> girls and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e9f9eb8f39820b3b8cd2c4b06e10d90e0d3b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> boys in the class, as the ratio of girls to boys is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/41281174060fd95dee9dac239ba24691436e388b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:5$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />. The total number of students in the class is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d6580941dc18adc3d16e0044e1ec5173128b5335.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 5x = 8x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>We know that the class has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students in total. Thus, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5cbf74e8a715aec84793c55ffa61323658cb98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8x = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690ef55a607beaf2389d1ee102df817721bc2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>There is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ace4c0c0c7d22db4722511833b50ec4d56548ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x - 3x = 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> fewer girls than boys, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/2/2c2b22c2aca4a686e0cb7cfeddec8ab236f4e86b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"123\" height=\"30\" /> fewer girls.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Gr